# nr-office-raster-svg: SVG rasterisation in mixdog-raster (module svg, tests/twin_svg.rs, fixtures/office-svg)

Not compiled: cargo was not run (the lead compiles the wave). Everything below is a paste.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-raster/src/lib.rs

After `pub mod stats;` / `pub mod canvas;` in the module list add:

    pub mod svg;

After `pub use crate::stats::stats;` add:

    pub use crate::svg::Logo;
    pub use crate::svg::SvgFonts;
    pub use crate::svg::SvgMetadata;

## native/core/crates/mixdog-raster/Cargo.toml

[dependencies], after the `mixdog-rt` line (the same exact version and features as mixdog-imaging's entry, so nothing new is resolved;
resvg re-exports usvg, usvg's roxmltree and fontdb and tiny-skia, which svg.rs uses through it):

    resvg = { version = "=0.45.1", default-features = false, features = ["text", "system-fonts", "raster-images"] }

## native/core/Cargo.lock and mixdog-workspace-hack

`cargo update --workspace --offline` adds `"resvg",` to the dependencies of the package mixdog-raster (no new package: resvg 0.45.1 and
its tree are locked for mixdog-imaging). Run `cargo hakari generate` / the hakari check: the features of resvg are the ones mixdog-imaging
already unifies, so no change is expected.

